    "authorAssociation": "NONE",
    "body": "I have the following mapping, which allows me to pad pairs (e.g., `(|)` + `space` -> `( | )` :\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nmappings = {\r\n  [\" \"] = { \r\n    action = \"closeopen\",\r\n    pair = \"  \",\r\n    neigh_pattern = \"[%(%[{][%)%]}]\",\r\n  },\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis works great and allows me to use another `space` to get to the closing `)` and then hit `)` to exit, which, generally, is usually what I want. BUT - the `space` to get to the `)` is both a wasted keystroke, and a bit confusing. What I'd really like is to be able to be in this position `( | )`, hit `)` and move to `(  )|`.\r\n\r\nThis will also allow me to convert the above rule from `closeopen` to just open.\r\n\r\nIs this at all possible?",
    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">I have the following mapping, which allows me to pad pairs (e.g., <code class=\"notranslate\">(|)</code> + <code class=\"notranslate\">space</code> -&gt; <code class=\"notranslate\">( | )</code> :</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-lua notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"mappings = {\n  [&quot; &quot;] = { \n    action = &quot;closeopen&quot;,\n    pair = &quot;  &quot;,\n    neigh_pattern = &quot;[%(%[{][%)%]}]&quot;,\n  },\n}\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-smi\">mappings</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> {\n  [<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span> <span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>] <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> { \n    <span class=\"pl-smi\">action</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>closeopen<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>,\n    <span class=\"pl-smi\">pair</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>  <span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>,\n    <span class=\"pl-smi\">neigh_pattern</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>[%(%[{][%)%]}]<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>,\n  },\n}</pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This works great and allows me to use another <code class=\"notranslate\">space</code> to get to the closing <code class=\"notranslate\">)</code> and then hit <code class=\"notranslate\">)</code> to exit, which, generally, is usually what I want. BUT - the <code class=\"notranslate\">space</code> to get to the <code class=\"notranslate\">)</code> is both a wasted keystroke, and a bit confusing. What I'd really like is to be able to be in this position <code class=\"notranslate\">( | )</code>, hit <code class=\"notranslate\">)</code> and move to <code class=\"notranslate\">(  )|</code>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This will also allow me to convert the above rule from <code class=\"notranslate\">closeopen</code> to just open.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Is this at all possible?</p>",
    "bodyText": "I have the following mapping, which allows me to pad pairs (e.g., (|) + space -> ( | ) :\nmappings = {\n  [\" \"] = { \n    action = \"closeopen\",\n    pair = \"  \",\n    neigh_pattern = \"[%(%[{][%)%]}]\",\n  },\n}\nThis works great and allows me to use another space to get to the closing ) and then hit ) to exit, which, generally, is usually what I want. BUT - the space to get to the ) is both a wasted keystroke, and a bit confusing. What I'd really like is to be able to be in this position ( | ), hit ) and move to (  )|.\nThis will also allow me to convert the above rule from closeopen to just open.\nIs this at all possible?",
